 "text": "Home\n/\nGovernment\n/\n Departments\n/\n Library and Community Services\n/\nActivity guide\nActivity guide\nLearning is a lifelong adventure! The City of Menlo Park hosts a wide range of high-quality recreational classes. Fitness, dance, sports, gymnastics, music, drama, arts, crafts, cooking, and much more. Whether you're a curious newcomer or a seasoned student, there's probably something to pique your interest.\nPlease note the following changes as part of balancing the \nCity's budget for fiscal year 2026-27\n:\n- Credit and debit card processing fees are now passed directly to the cardholder.\n- Burgess Pool and Belle Haven Pool have \nnew hours\n.\n- Gymnastics class fees have increased as part of the \nCity's Fiscal Year \n2026-27 Master Fee Schedule\n.\n-\nWe transitioned to a new payment processor. Some previously saved payment methods may no longer work during online checkout. If you experience an issue, please select \"Add a New Card\" and enter your credit card information again. For security purposes, the billing address and ZIP code you enter must exactly match the information your credit card issuer has on file, or your payment may be declined.\nPlease note the following upcoming closures:\n- The City of Menlo Park's Library and Community Services facilities will be closed on Wednesday, Nov. 11, for Veterans Day. We will resume our regularly held business hours the following day. \nFall 2026 Classes and Camps\nTo view \nonly\n classes located at Belle Haven Community Campus, \nclick here\n.\nAll\nYouth\nCamps\nAdult\nAdults 60+\nGymnastics\nAquatics\nAll\nEmbedding Example\nYouth\nEmbedding Example\nCamps\nEmbedding Example\nAdult\nEmbedding Example\nAdults 60+\nEmbedding Example\nGymnastics\nEmbedding Example\nAquatics\nMenlo Swim and the City of Menlo Park both use Xplor for our class registration systems. Remember to use the correct login and password for each account. Menlo Swim and the City of Menlo Park both value your privacy—we don’t share your login information with anyone, not even each other.\nPress left and right keys to move between tabs. Press down to focus tab content.\nIf the above listings are currently unavailable to view on this webpage, \nplease click here to view classes and facility rentals directly from our online registration system.\nActivity Guide enrollment dates\nSign up for our weekly Library and Community Services newsletter\n to be the first to hear about enrollment dates!\nPrevious column\nNext column\nActivity\nHyperlocal resident*\nMenlo Park resident\nNon-resident/ Unincorporated\n Fall 2026\n Now open\nNow open\n Now open\n Winter 2027**\n December (TBD)**\n December (TBD)**\n December (TBD)**\nWhat is a hyperlocal resident*?\n Menlo Park residents or students who attend a K-12 school within \nthe service area of Belle Haven Community Campus\n (BHCC) are eligible for discounted enrollment fees at BHCC. Students who attend school in the BHCC service area\n but do not live in Menlo Park may submit a \nhyperlocal student information form\nto enroll at the hyperlocal resident rate.\nWhen does enrollment open?\n The City of Menlo Park has season-based recreation enrollment periods. Although specific dates vary each year, the anticipated enrollment months are shown in the table above. **Finalized dates will be announced as soon as available.\nRecreation scholarships\nTo reduce barriers posed by enrollment fees, the recreation scholarship policy provides discounted enrollment fees to qualifying low- and moderate-income residents. Please fill out an interest form if you think you qualify for a recreation scholarship. Click here to read the full \nRecreation Scholarship Policy.\n(PDF, 175KB)\nFill out the Recreation Scholarship Interest form\nContact us\nNeed help enrolling?\n No problem! City staff are available in person and by phone at libraries and recreation facilities to help.\nEmail: \nregistration@menlopark.gov\nArrillaga Family Recreation Center\n700 Alma St.\n650-330-2200\nArrillaga Family Gymnasium\n600 Alma St.\n650-330-2220\nArrillaga Family Gymnastics Center\n501 Laurel St.\n650-330-2224\nBelle Haven Community Campus\n100 Terminal Ave.\n650-330-2205\nBelle Haven Pool\nMenlo Swim & Sport\n100 Terminal Ave.\n650-781-5525\nBurgess Pool\nMenlo Swim & Sport\n501 Laurel St.\n650-781-5525\nRelated Information\nRecreation and sports\nEvents\nMenlo Park Senior Center\nAthletic fields\nParks\nShare\nFacebook\nX\nEmail\nPrint\nLinkedIn\nBack to top",
